"page": "$ARCIRCLE page",
"title": "Questions people ask.",
"url": "/arcircle",
"text": "What is the contract address? — on Arc (chain 5042). Always check it on ArcScan ↗ before you trade. Where can I buy it? On Argus, where it launched. It trades in a Uniswap v4 pool on Arc, so it also shows up on Dexscreener and other trackers that index Arc — always check the contract address first. Has any $ARCIRCLE been burned? Yes. Two team burns started it — 116,772,290.56 $ARCIRCLE on 25 September 2026 and 9,491,742.10 on 26 September 2026 — and every vote, Token Scanner unlock, Builder Mine join and secret-file opening has burned more since. All of it sits at the dead address 0x000…dEaD, which no one controls. The live total is shown above, and every burn by source is on the Reward page. What can I do with $ARCIRCLE? Vote on CirclePad rounds, unlock Token Scanner Plus and Pro tools, join and gear up on Builder Mine (with a payout bonus for holding 100K / 1M / 5M), open ARCIA's secret file, and hold 100,000+ to receive Relay launches. See What $ARCIRCLE does. What is the burn engine? A reward contract, being built, that takes utility and platform revenue and buys back and burns $ARCIRCLE and $ARCIA automatically. Contract details, burn ratios and the timeline are shared as each piece is ready. Follow it on the Reward page → How is $ARCIA related? $ARCIA is CirclePad Round #1's coin, named after ARCIA and chosen by the community. It joins $ARCIRCLE in the reward contract's automated buyback-and-burn. Its contract: 0x9da6d5ce413e94264Ea411372459413334a83bE5. Is the liquidity locked? Yes. Argus puts the whole supply into a single Uniswap v4 position when the pool is created and hands it to a locker contract that has no withdraw function — nobody, Argus included, can pull that liquidity. Is there a team allocation? No. Argus put all 1,000,000,000 $ARCIRCLE into the pool's liquidity position at launch; there is no separate team allocation. The supply split above shows where it sits today. What is the creator fee? Every $ARCIRCLE trade pays the launch's buy or sell tax — set once at launch between 1% and 10%, and fixed forever — on top of the 1% pool fee. Argus keeps 10% of the tax; the other 90% goes to the creator's allocation, in USDC. That share is one of the revenue sources that feed the flywheel. Do holders get rewards? A reward program for holders and creators is planned, funded by ecosystem revenue — never by new tokens — alongside the burn engine being built. Nothing is promised until its rules are published on the Reward page. $ARCIRCLE is a community memecoin on Circle's Arc chain. Nothing on this page is financial advice or a promise of returns. The flywheel describes how ARCIRCLE PAD intends to use its revenue; details are published here as each part goes live. Crypto is volatile — only use what you can afford to lose."
