"text": "Every report comes with a call for the next 24 hours: Safe, Caution or Risky. The call is recorded with a hash before the outcome exists, then graded from the market: it \"went bad\" if the price fell 60% or more, or the liquidity 50% or more. A Safe call is right if it didn't go bad; a Risky call is right if it did. Caution isn't graded. One call per token every 12 hours. The Record tab shows every call and the hit rate. A call is about risk, never about price direction. It's not a signal to buy or sell anything. Once a day, ARCIA writes the previous day's call hashes on Arc as one root, from her own wallet. The Record tab re-computes that root in your browser and compares it with the transaction, so anyone can check the calls were made before their outcomes."
