"title": "Questions about rewards.",
"url": "/reward",
"text": "Are rewards live? Not yet. Burns are live today in every utility; the reward contract and the holder and creator programs are being built, and they only go live once their rules are published on this page. What is the burn engine? A reward contract that receives utility and platform revenue and buys back and burns $ARCIRCLE and $ARCIA automatically, so no one has to press a button. The core framework is being built; contract details, burn ratios and the rollout timeline are shared as each piece is ready. How are burns labeled by source? Each transfer to 0x…dEaD is matched to its transaction: the contract it called (burn-to-vote, Builder Mine, ARCIA DESK), or the Token Scanner unlock or secret file it paid for. Anything else is shown as a direct burn from a wallet. Do I need to do anything now? No. There is nothing to register or claim today. The wallet check above only shows the on-chain activity the programs are designed around. Will buying just before a snapshot help? The candidate design uses time-weighted balances and unannounced snapshots, so a balance held for a moment counts for very little. Where does the money come from? From what the ecosystem earns: the five revenue sources above. No new $ARCIRCLE is ever minted to pay rewards. Does my vote in the poll decide the design? It is a signal, not a binding vote. It shows which mechanics the community cares about while the rules are being written. Is holding $ARCIRCLE a claim on revenue? No. $ARCIRCLE is a community memecoin — holding it is not a share, a claim on revenue or a right to any payment. Commitments"
